From ead804ed19967b6d1ae639833693026cb7a272f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:25:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] nvk/rm: GPU VA allocation and binding

NVK keeps choosing every GPU address from its own util_vma_heap (with the
replay heap for capture/replay).  Each nvkmd_va is backed by an
NV50_MEMORY_VIRTUAL that RM allocates at exactly that address
(FIXED_ADDRESS_ALLOCATE), with NVOS32_ALLOC_FLAGS_SPARSE for sparse
ranges.  If RM already has something there, the range stays reserved in
our heap and another one is tried.

Binding maps the memory into that virtual object with
NV_ESC_RM_MAP_MEMORY_DMA and DMA_OFFSET_FIXED (absolute VA), 64 KiB pages
for VRAM and snooped 4 KiB pages for system memory, and the VA's PTE kind
through kindOverride when librmclient has crm_map_dma2.  RM unmaps whole
mappings only, so each VA tracks its mappings and a partial unbind
unmaps the overlapping ones and maps back the remainders.

